# Python pytest cache (the GDScript-via-pytest CI tests)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# FEAT-360 (resolves DEF-VER-001): def001_gate_captured_output.log is a
# GENERATED artifact -- tests/integration/test_def001_gate_evidence.py's
# `captured_evidence_log` fixture rewrites it on EVERY real run of that
# suite (raw stdout/stderr from both the nested `pytest` run and the real
# `godot ... --gut-run-all` run), and it used to live at the git-TRACKED
# tests/integration/fixtures/def001_gate_captured_output.log path. That
# meant every run of the DEF-001 gate suite left the working tree dirty --
# exactly the class of regression scripts/verify_clean_tree.sh's
# clean_tree_gate exists to catch (peer review finding DEF-VER-001).
#
# The fix mirrors FEAT-292's sim_results.json precedent below: the log is
# now written to a dedicated, root-anchored, git-ignored `.test-output/`
# directory instead of the tracked fixtures/ path (see
# tests/integration/test_def001_gate_evidence.py's
# CAPTURED_EVIDENCE_LOG_PATH), and the old tracked copy has been removed
# from the git index (`git rm`). Root-anchored and scoped to its own
# directory name so it can never shadow tests/integration/fixtures/'s
# other, legitimately committed fixtures (gut_output_known_good.txt,
# gut_output_regressed.txt, baseline_out_of_scope_hashes.json) -- see
# tests/ci/test_def001_gate_log_gitignore_feat360.py.
/.test-output/

# FEAT-292 (resolves PR-001/PR-002): sim_results.json is a GENERATED
# artifact — tests/sim/test_balance_sim.gd (core/sim/simulator.gd's N=1000
# balance regression) rewrites res://sim_results.json on every single test
# run, and two of its seven keys (commit_hash, timestamp) change on every
# regen even when nothing balance-relevant moved. It used to be committed
# to git, which meant `scripts/test_command.sh` (and its N=1000 stage
# specifically) left the working tree dirty after every run — a
# CLAUDE.md commit-hygiene / deployment-gate violation, since nobody was
# ever meant to hand-commit a fresh commit_hash/timestamp pair every time
# the suite executes.
#
# The file stays at its existing res://sim_results.json (repo root) path —
# scripts/ci/check_sim_results_provenance.py, tests/pytest/
# test_sim_results_provenance.py, and .github/workflows/test.yml's
# artifact-upload step all read/write it there — but it is no longer
# tracked by git. Anchored to the repo root (leading `/`) and matched by
# exact filename only, so this rule can never shadow any data/*.tres
# resource file (per CLAUDE.md, data/ files must remain trackable/
# committed) — see tests/ci/test_sim_results_gitignore_feat292.py.
/sim_results.json
